# bench --archive-runs output (src/bench/archive.ts): a results directory in bench/results now
# archives its runs' records by default, ~4 MB gz per 22-task slice. The un-ignore rules above
# would otherwise commit them on every bench run. A record archive is checked in DELIBERATELY and
# as one file, the way experiments/results/oos-2026-09-22-runs.tar.gz was.
bench/results/*/runs/
!bench/results/iter1-*/
!bench/results/iter2-*/

# iteration 2's harvested run transcripts (experiments/results/llm-jev-iter2.md §10 defect 1): the warm plane's
# counters — disabledReason, fallbacks, restarts, screen:mismatch — exist ONLY as free text in the sieve's
# `synth · verify` event, and `--archive-runs` does not copy transcript.log. They are the sole evidence for the
# warm A/B, so the global `*.log` rule is lifted for exactly these directories (1.7 MB of text, checked in
# deliberately). Delete the rule once the counters reach SearchTrace.
!bench/results/iter2-*/transcripts/*.log
